      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Clinical trials for the most effective drugs in the armamentarium of medications for inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) have shown only a 50-60% response rate, and this drops to 30% in maintenance. However, therapeutic drug monitoring (TDM) to adjust dosing to account for patient-specific characteristics, which has been shown to improve outcomes, was not utilized in these trials. This review will detail the development of TDM within the IBD space as it evolved from thiopurines to biologics and continues to evolve with loftier treat-to-target goals and more sophisticated dashboard systems."
      },
